payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    loom/schema/component.js — COMPONENT_SCHEMA (real, checked directly this pass:
    requiredKeys ['id','namespace','name','version'], uuid enforced separately by the
    loom.uuid-present Axiom in driver.js, not duplicated here). Broadened this pass, on request:
    a component is deliberately language/syntax-agnostic already — the real schema never assumed
    JS specifically, id/namespace/name/version says nothing about what's inside. `boundary` added
    as an optional field, grounded in cos/kernel.js's real Compartment class — its own `axioms`
    (1-5 identity-defining invariants, immutable, enforced: "Compartment requires at least one
    axiom... max 5 — keep identity tight") is the real precedent for "a component as a compartment
    with boundaries." Not merged into `.cos` — a cos Compartment is a live, running, stateful thing
    (gates, buses, context); a `.component` node is a static declaration. Same boundary concept,
    borrowed field, two different real things. Clear-glass's own use: clear-glass.node-taxonomy.md
    marks this VIA LOOM, confirmed — both 'clear-glass' and 'clear-glass/seam' are separate real
    entries in capability-map.js's own SYSTEMS map, so both get their components derived the same
    way guardian's are. This local copy exists so clear-glass can validate/interpret component-shaped
    data it receives back from that derivation without a runtime dependency on lib/node-schemas.js —
    same reasoning already applied to clear-glass's other VIA LOOM types (hook, wire, node), which
    already had local copies before this one.
  fields:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, unique component id
    namespace:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real component namespace
    name:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real component display/file name
    version:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real semver-ish version string
    dir:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: optional real filesystem path, added by SB1
    uuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: enforced by the loom.uuid-present Axiom, not this schema directly
    boundary:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: >-
        optional 1-5 identity-defining invariants for this component, same real concept as
        cos/kernel.js's Compartment.axioms — what this component IS and is NOT, bounding its
        scope regardless of what language or syntax it's actually written in. Optional because
        most real components today declare none; a component using this is opting into being
        treated like a bounded compartment, not just a named, versioned file.
